summary: 'Addressed PR #52 merge blockers on feat/gnomon-windows (7f4073e1, bc227d58, a709d871); CI now green on all 8 jobs. Blockers: win32SystemRoot replaces the ''C:\Windows'' literal (drive-rooted only, per Aegis); WINDOWS_EXTRA gated to win32 with a darwin test; strict device-key nlink proven intended on darwin/linux; partial sandbox fidelity reaches status and the win32 deny table claims only built mechanisms; rust-toolchain.toml pins 1.93.1. Windows CI root cause took three layers on the elevated-admin runner: (1) new objects owned by BA -> helper sets owner to the user; (2) the runner is the built-in Administrator, which SDDL spells LA -> verdicts compare in the SDDL spelling (info.userSddlSid); (3) children created by the kernel still BA-owned -> new helper op process.owner-default sets the token''s default owner to its user. Ubuntu self-update-e2e was pre-existing on feat/gnomon (linux has no transport profile, gui.open refuses) and is now scoped to darwin. Aegis approved each step.'
